String reverse(String s) {
    char[] c = s.toCharArray();
    int i = 0, j = c.length - 1;
    while (i < j) {
        char tmp = c[i];        // swap ends
        c[i] = c[j];
        c[j] = tmp;
        i++; j--;               // move inward
    }
    return new String(c);
}

// "java" -> c = [j,a,v,a]
// i=0,j=3: swap -> [a,a,v,j]; i=1,j=2: swap -> [a,v,a,j]; i=2,j=1 stop
// result: "avaj"
```
Without the manual rule, `new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString()` does the same in one line - but interviewers usually want the loop.

